cast-auth.json — Google Cast device-authentication credentials

This file is data, not AirShow source code, and is not covered by AirShow's
license. It contains a Google Cast device certificate, its intermediate
certificate, an RSA private key, and a table of precomputed signatures. They
were extracted from the AirReceiver Android app and published by the shanocast
project (https://github.com/rgerganov/shanocast), which carries no license.
AirShow's authors did not create this data and cannot grant any rights to it.

Without credentials like these, Chrome and Android refuse to cast to a receiver.
Redistributing or using them may be restricted by Google's or the AirReceiver
developers' rights; anyone shipping this file is responsible for checking that
themselves.

The signature table covers 2023-08-15 to 2027-12-21 (UTC). After that, Cast
stops working unless a newer cast-auth.json is supplied — via the
AIRSHOW_CAST_AUTH environment variable or a cast-auth.json in AirShow's app
data directory (format documented in src/cast/CastAuth.h).
